    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What does ASTA Color Value measure?</h3>
      <p>ASTA measures the extractable carotenoid pigments — chiefly capsanthin — that give paprika its red colour, quantified at 460 nm by ASTA Method 20.1. It measures colour, not heat, flavour or freshness.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What is the difference between ASTA and SHU?</h3>
      <p>ASTA measures colour (carotenoids such as capsanthin); SHU measures heat (capsaicinoids). They are independent — a paprika can be high-ASTA and zero-heat.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Why does paprika colour fade?</h3>
      <p>Carotenoids degrade under oxygen, light and heat, and ASTA colour declines with age. Cool, dark, sealed storage and fresh lot turnover preserve colour.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>How is ASTA colour measured?</h3>
      <p>By acetone extraction and spectrophotometry at 460 nm (ASTA Method 20.1), then converting absorbance to ASTA units. IC colour is ASTA × 40.</p>
    </div>

